From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MyNaai Dev <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Booking requests (leads): salon tab API, admin tab API, the 60s window

Requests are NOT bookings. `booking_requests` is the lead a customer sent; the
`booking` / `booking_list` table holds the chair that exists after a salon
accepts. This patch adds the two lists the new tabs read, and keeps the two
concepts apart in every query: nothing here counts a request as a booking, and
the only link is the `booking_id` pointer written on accept.

  POST /api/bookingRequest/salon/list       { salonId?, status?, page?, limit?, fromDate?, toDate? }
  POST /api/bookingRequest/salon/summary    { salonId?, range? }  TODAY | WEEK | MONTH | ALL
  POST /api/bookingRequest/admin/list      { salonId?, status?, search?, page?, limit?, fromDate?, toDate? }
  POST /api/bookingRequest/admin/summary   { range?, salonId?, fromDate?, toDate? }

Answers use the house envelope. `salon/*` require a salon token and 403 on a
`salonId` that is not the caller's; `admin/*` require an admin token. The salon
list answers `{ requests, pagination: { page, limit, totalPages, totalRequests } }`
with the row shape the website already reads (`bookingRequestId`, `customerName`,
`customerPhone`, `bookingDate`, `bookingTime`, `barberName`, `status`, `createdAt`,
`expiresAt`, `respondedAt`, `bookingId`, `services[]`). The admin list adds
`salonName`, `salonPhone`, `city`, `responseSeconds` and `outcome`
(`answered | missed | withdrawn | open`).

Counting, which is the whole point of the tabs:

  · `autoCancelled` is its own bucket — never folded into `rejected`. A salon that
    misses leads has a staffing problem; a salon that rejects them has a pricing
    one.
  · a customer's own cancellation (`CANCELLED`) is a third bucket,
    `cancelledByCustomer`, and is never counted as a missed lead.
  · `answerRate = round((accepted + rejected) / received * 100)`; the buckets add
    up to `received`.
  · `admin/summary` adds `bySalon` (received / accepted / rejected / missed /
    answerRate / `medianResponseSeconds` from `percentile_cont(0.5)` in SQL) and
    a `platform` block. Salons that never answered have a null median — the panel
    shows a dash, not a zero, because a zero reads as "instant reply".

The answer window

  · `POST /bookingRequest/create-booking-request` now stamps `expires_at` =
    created + 60s, SERVER-side. A client never sends it.
  · `expires_at` / `responded_at` / `booking_id` / `routed_barber_id` are added
    to the model and to the migration.
  · `ownerAction` writes `responded_at` on accept and reject, writes `booking_id`
    when the booking row exists (inside the same transaction — the old code saved
    that booking outside it), and refuses a request past its window with
    "This request has expired and was cancelled automatically". A second accept
    answers "This request was already actioned".
  · `cron/bookingRequestSweeper.cron.js` runs every 20 seconds and writes
    `status = 'AUTO_CANCELLED', responded_at = expires_at` for every PENDING row
    past its window, then notifies the customer (slot released) and the salon
    (missed, expressly not "rejected"). Idempotent: the `WHERE status = 'PENDING'`
    clause means a second run finds nothing.
  · the list and summary endpoints also derive the state per row, so a tab opened
    between two cron ticks never offers an Accept that cannot succeed.

Files

  new  src/services/bookingRequestLead.service.js     the lists, the counters, the sweep
  new  src/controller/bookingRequest/listSalonBookingRequests.js
  new  src/controller/bookingRequest/salonBookingRequestSummary.js
  new  src/controller/bookingRequest/adminListBookingRequests.js
  new  src/controller/bookingRequest/adminBookingRequestSummary.js
  new  cron/bookingRequestSweeper.cron.js
  mod  src/database/models/bookingRequest.model.js    window + outcome columns
  mod  src/controller/bookingRequest/bookingRequest.js  stamp expires_at on create
  mod  src/controller/bookingRequest/ownerAction.js     responded_at, booking_id,
                                                        expired refusal, tx fix
  mod  src/routes/bookingRequest.routes.js              the four new doors
  mod  index.js                                         boot-time schema guard +
                                                        start the sweeper

Apply after backend-1-shop-categories (this imports its `ensureShopSchema`).

Verified: `node --check` on every file; `bookingRequest.routes` loads with all
nine routes; the pure parts were exercised against a stub ORM — effective status
(an expired PENDING reads AUTO_CANCELLED, an ACCEPTED stays ACCEPTED), the
services snapshot and ₹ total, `responseSeconds`, `outcome`, the three filter
clauses (PENDING excludes expired; AUTO_CANCELLED includes both written and
expired-but-unwritten), and TODAY starting at IST midnight.
